{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346889-lvl-1-spheres-effects-ideas","id":1346889,"title":"Lvl 1 spheres effects ideas","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-07T16:21:00-08:00","id":1346889,"title":"Lvl 1 spheres effects ideas","content":"Post here some good ideas and intelligent ways of using the first dot the spheres. I would really like to see suggestions of Forces, Life and Prime spheres, but feel free to post about any other too.<br /> <br /> Here's what I already got:<br /> <br /> Forces: Getting all electromagnectic wave spectrum: infrared (see in dark and hidden targets), radio (frequency to hear police radio or spy cellphone calls), dark light, Sonar, Superhuman vision/hearing (reduce diff to perception rolls).<br /> <br /> Life: Detecting the presence of Life in the area, detecting undead, detecting wonds/disease/poison in someone, see alterations in hormones/body behaviour to detect target intentions (lie, attack,run,etc.), read target characteristics (age,sex,health,etc.).<br /> <br /> <br /> Prime: Detect use of magick, read ressonance and signatures, absotrb more than avatar rating of Quintessence, consecrate objects, infuse personal Quintessence, countermagick, turn health lvl into Quintessence.<br /> <br /> I listed the basic and I am eager to read other uses of them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T17:42:59-08:00","id":1346906,"title":"","content":"Entropy: Sensing a particular pattern when seeing a teen skateboarding toward himself, Marcus wanting to do a little &quot;prank&quot; coincidentally turns around suddenly just at the right moment possible to make the boy go crashing through a window. This is because the Trenchcoat Marcus was wearing was long enough to shift wind that was carrying rock pebbles that went straight into the kid's eye.<br /> <br /> Mind: Johnny Bravo uses Mind to tell if the current girl that he is flirting with likes him or not. The Effect worked, but the girl doesn't like him that much.<br /> <br /> Time: With knowing the exact second of time almost every time since Awakening, Robert never procrastinates anymore getting carried away with gaming too often. Now he can finally do his college projects on time- maybe that was the reason why he Awakened?<br /> <br /> Matter: Working at a Pawnshop, Carl knows whether the product being haggled is either fake or not.<br /> <br /> Spirit: Being bored at the Mall with his girlfriend, Ja'Quan peers into through the Gauntlet to see whats happening in this Forever 21 store. Nothing seemed out of the ordinary, until he spotted a chilling sight, pun intended. A giant 6'4 Yeti Umbrood stands next to the cute cashier manning the giant line that was slowly former up. Its fur is so white and bright that Ja'Quan's had to partially shield his eyes before adjusting to it. Where there was no fur incurred on the body of this Umbrood, it would have light blue-skin that looks leathery, but soft at the same-time. Most fearful of the thing is that it has shining bright crimson eyes. The thing stands protectively next to the girl, massive beefed up arms crossed. Suddenly it turns, staring deep into the very eyes of Ja'Quan stabbing an intense pang of fear into the heart of Ja'Quan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T18:15:35-08:00","id":1346909,"title":"","content":"I think the entropy one requires more than 1 dot.. <br /> <br /> Nice examples, though. Any thoughts on the spheres I posted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T18:43:42-08:00","id":1346912,"title":"","content":"Forces: Jerry Seinfeld has Awakened yesterday, but finds it hard to control his Primary Sphere Force on when it takes Effect and when it shouldn't. He keeps perceiving all the energy fluctuations of all the TVs in the apartment complex almost 24/7 and it is deteriorating his mental health. What Seinfeld doesn't know is that Kramer is a Arete 5 Marauder master who was exuberant when sensed he that Jerry was a Mage and has been cultivating his madness subtly since yesterday with Mind 5 and Forces 5 to enhance Jerry's Primary Sphere for his benefit of turning him to the forces of the Wlyd.<br /> <br /> Life: Being a construction worker in Egypt is hard, but Akhmed does what he has to do. In a few hours of constructing a park funded by a the Government, he has an innate sense to see one of his fellow worker extremely hot.. More hot than a human could ever be. The co-worker looks back to Akhmed and smiles coyly. Akhmed could swear he saw a fiery gleam in the eyes of the man, but the co-worker turns back to his work shoveling out some sand to make way for a Merry-Go-Around<br /> <br /> Prime: Jimmy Awakened while walking home to school and despite that short time, he immediately knew the meaning of Prime as his Primary Sphere, if only a much as the boy could gleam as mere novice. Just at the right moment while passing a Bakery, he senses a very short man chant something, allowim him to partially see somesort of glimmer sprinkle on a couple loaves of bread. &quot;What the heck was that?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":25523,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","user":"Shakanaka","date":". 11-07-2019, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T19:10:10-08:00","id":1346918,"title":"","content":"Soo, tv signals, body temperature (disease?) and magick use?<br /> <br /> Those were in the OP...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T20:00:57-08:00","id":1346928,"title":"","content":"Whoops I got confused.<br /> <br /> Forces: Everything is correct with Sphere 1 Forces.<br /> <br /> Life: I don't know about detecting Undead.. Since Undead are.. Dead. Did you mean whether or not the Mage can sense something is off with somebody who seems to be standing and walking around, but should be dead?<br /> <br /> Prime: What did you mean by absorb more than avatar rating of Quintessence?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-07T20:06:49-08:00","id":1346931,"title":"","content":"Use life magick to detect how alive someone is. You use it on an undead. Since undead traditionally require Life + matter to effect them, you probably pick up they have some life force but so little they should be clinically dead. Congrats you detect a vampire. Or it flat out doesn't work, I'd let it pick up someone is dead or alive. <br /> <br /> <br /> Prime: You need prime 1 if you want to store more quintessence than your Avatar. Say you have an Avatar of 3. Without Prime 1, your max quintessence is 3. With prime 1 you can meditate at a node and get more than 3 (I forget if you technically even cast while doing this or if it's base meditation). This is a base effect in the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T06:59:21-08:00","id":1347008,"title":"","content":"*Much like with Life 1 you can sense the target characteristics (assuming a living target), Forces 1 allows to sense the properties of energies. For instance: By watching the Forces released by a weapon you could (with the correct Knowledges) estimate how much damage the weapon does.<br /> <br /> *Movement it's cinetic energy, so you could also use Forces 1 to &quot;sense movement&quot; in the area, and to judge how fast or how slow it is.<br /> <br /> One interesting thing about lvl 1 Spheres it's that you can *share* your senses too. It takes more than one success, and it's Vulgar when doing so to mundanes (unless it can be explained somehow, like giving them weird looking lenses or drugs).<br /> Now, when one thinks &quot;sensory effects&quot; one often thinks about things that would be useful or beneficial to perceive (and surely this can be used that way to help your people), but when affecting others <i>it's also feasible to use this offensively</i> showing the target stuff that, while 100% real, it's horrifying or just distracting. It may be a curse even.<br /> For instance, once a character of mine gave an enemy human assassin the power to see and hear ghosts (not the power to *unsee* them, though). At that moment the ghost of someone he had recently killed was there (and not in a nice mood). Was pretty funny. Needless to say, he reacted like he had seen a ghost :P .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-08-2019, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T11:23:06-08:00","id":1347072,"title":"","content":"Adding to what Aleph said about using level 1 spheres offensively by tossing the perception onto somebody else.. (Just note that, at least according to HDYDT you also need Mind 3 to do it to an unwilling target in sight..)<br /> <br /> Forces. The forces sphere is insanely good for distracting the hell out of people. Make them *see* sound and radio waves. We have so much sound and all sorts of wireless communications in urban and city environments, that if the enemy is not used to sensing them this way, and especially if you pile such things up at once, it will be like pointing a stroboscope at their face - sensory overload all the way.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T12:01:00-08:00","id":1347076,"title":"","content":"Let's not forget about Correspondence 1. It essentially gives you 360 degree vision, an awareness of location/distance of any sensed target with other powers, And a perfect sense of location, direction and balance.<br /> <br /> A person with correspondance 1 would have near-perfect aim, they'd be able to know exactly how far away a target is and what position they need to be in to hit it. Normal soldiers and archers have to train for years to get that same sense of distance.<br /> <br /> Another thing, by combining correspondence 1 with time 1 you can essentially allow a person can do something similar for melee combat, dancing and other athletic sports. They'd have a perfect sense of what position they and/or their opponent is in as well as a perfect sense of timing and rhythm for any action they need to perform.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 11-08-2019, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T14:19:45-08:00","id":1347099,"title":"","content":"Nice. You need to touch the target to give the visionz though.<br /> <br /> I wonder how a sense danger &quot;spider sense&quot; like could be done. Probably there are more than 1 way.<br /> I think it would require entropy. You think it is possible of something similar with the 3 spheres in OP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T16:01:43-08:00","id":1347119,"title":"","content":"I used to think that Time 1 was the worst first-rank Sphere. After I gave it more thought, I think you can extrapolate or at least justify more abilities from Time 1 than the core books give. For instance:<br /> <br /> -Eidetic memory<br /> -Knowing exactly how old a thing or process is<br /> -If you've traveled to the past, knowing what changes to avoid that would change too much and cause more Paradox<br /> -Perfect timing is probably its most powerful use since it can enhance a lot of mundane abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T17:55:46-08:00","id":1347144,"title":"","content":"Time 1 can let you do slipstream (Along with like every other sphere in the game) which is one of the best spells in the entire game. It's in HDYDT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T22:06:58-08:00","id":1347168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how a sense danger &quot;spider sense&quot; like could be done. Probably there are more than 1 way.<br /> I think it would require entropy. You think it is possible of something similar with the 3 spheres in OP?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's squarely on the realm of Entropy.<br /> <br /> I DO think you could do something approaching a spider sense with those 3 + Correspondence 1. The general idea would be to have your magick pasively scanning stuff and detecting energies, vectors of Force, so to speak, from the ambience, stuff, and people that would be able to hurt you, filtering those that come close so you sense only these (note that you wouldn't know for certain that these &quot;vectors&quot; <i>are </i>going to hurt you w/o Entropy or Time 2). It should require a number of successes to do all that, and Correspondence it's necessary to englobe stuff you aren't currently sensing (avoid sensory overload)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346889-lvl-1-spheres-effects-ideas?p=1347072#post1347072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adding to what Aleph said about using level 1 spheres offensively by tossing the perception onto somebody else.. (Just note that, at least according to HDYDT you also need Mind 3 to do it to an unwilling target in sight..)</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nice. You need to touch the target to give the visionz though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I forgot about that. This use is an outlier of the sensory effects. Understandably, it has been ruled differently in different editions. It's not very relevant, but I can't avoid the temptation to point out how much those limitations seem like an aftertought:<br /> <br /> Like, I could understand if somebody told me that Mind 2-3 telepathy it's necessary to share perceptions <i>at all</i>...but <i>since when</i> <i>the willingness of the target alters the Spheres needed</i> <i>to cast an Effect</i>. Even in Mind (the sphere that cares about this stuff), an unwilling target just adds to the difficulty (and gets a saving throw). This is not the most outrageous Sphere Tax of HDYDT, but it may be the oddest.<br /> <br /> The requisite to touch the target OR add Mind it's also bizarre. Other than spells with AoE (that was always a tricky subject) the range of all magick it's &quot;self&quot;, &quot;sensory range&quot; or &quot;Correspondence&quot;. As far as I remember, there isn't a D&amp;D-like &quot;touch range&quot; in Mage (unless your Paradigm says so, of course). Except for this one form of magick, apparently.<br /> <br /> <u>Professor </u> - there, assistant! , I can see the alien lifeform of type 3 we've been looking for. Of course, you can't see it without my special lenses. I will lend you my Ether Goggles so you can watch it, it's magnificent!<br /> <u>Assistant</u>: Puts on the goggles - Yes professor, I can see it!<br /> <u>Assistant</u> ... eh, professor?<br /> <u>Professor</u> ...yes assistant?<br /> <u>Assistant</u> ...why are you grabbing me? ... it's uncomfortable<br /> <u>Professor</u> - Oh shut up!, it's to transmit you the SCIENCE!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-09-2019, 01:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-08T23:28:59-08:00","id":1347176,"title":"","content":"Yes, the inconsistency is a weird thing.<br /> <br /> Personally, I *would* understand the requirement of at least Mind 2 to project the sensory magic into other people's minds as a default - to me it's more strange that Level 1 spheres would allow you to change other people's perceptions willy-nilly without it, to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T13:07:02-08:00","id":1347318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346889-lvl-1-spheres-effects-ideas?p=1347176#post1347176\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I *would* understand the requirement of at least Mind 2 to project the sensory magic into other people's minds as a default - to me it's more strange that Level 1 spheres would allow you to change other people's perceptions willy-nilly without it, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, to need some sort of &quot;projection&quot; Sphere to do this would make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> I don't know why Satyros decided not to make it like that by default. Maybe it was a nod to some previous material allowing it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-09-2019, 04:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-09T20:07:54-08:00","id":1347386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346889-lvl-1-spheres-effects-ideas?p=1347168#post1347168\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's squarely on the realm of Entropy.<br /> <br /> I DO think you could do something approaching a spider sense with those 3 + Correspondence 1. The general idea would be to have your magick pasively scanning stuff and detecting energies, vectors of Force, so to speak, from the ambience, stuff, and people that would be able to hurt you, filtering those that come close so you sense only these (note that you wouldn't know for certain that these &amp;quot;vectors&amp;quot; <i>are </i>going to hurt you w/o Entropy or Time 2). It should require a number of successes to do all that, and Correspondence it's necessary to englobe stuff you aren't currently sensing (avoid sensory overload)</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea! I don't see the need of correspondence, unless the mage wants to scan someplace (or someone) far away.<br /> I think this is doable only with Forces: you scan any energy that os directed at you with the potential to cause damage. So, a dart flying towards your head? Field scan that kinetic energy directly at you. Flamethrower spitting flame to your butt (or a rival mage's fireball)? Scans thermal energy heading your way. If we think right, every kind of damage has one kind of energy scaneable by Forces.<br /> What would Life be for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T04:47:38-08:00","id":1347656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346889-lvl-1-spheres-effects-ideas?p=1347386#post1347386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is doable only with Forces: you scan any energy that os directed at you with the potential to cause damage. So, a dart flying towards your head? Field scan that kinetic energy directly at you. Flamethrower spitting flame to your butt (or a rival mage's fireball)? Scans thermal energy heading your way. If we think right, every kind of damage has one kind of energy scaneable by Forces.<br /> What would Life be for?</div> </div> </div> </div>2 reasons.<br /> <br /> 1\u00ba Because you want to automagically filter the Forces patterns that would be able to harm you, Life takes care of that *you* element for you. Otherwise you would need to be sensing the intensity of all incoming Forces and judging them <i>by yourself.</i><br /> <br /> Now, there's a bajillon of Forces coming your way at every second (from the air movements to teluric vibrations, normally invisible radiations, and a big amount of etc.), the human mind isn't made to be hypersensitive to all of that all the time. Doing so would cause one hell of a sensory overload unlesss you can ignore most of it (in which case, it would be less effective to detect treaths. Like how we can detect light and sound, yet we have car accidents in spite of cars being big, bright and noisy. A functional danger sense would need to be intrusive enough to interrupt your walk in order to be useful)<br /> <br /> Besides, that's not what a spider sense *is* . That would be more akin to what Daredevil does, albeit more complex.<br /> <br /> 2\u00ba People wanting to punch you have to tense their muscles in a particular way. Forces interwoven with Life should detect this. To detect a <i>probably </i>incoming punch *before* the fist starts moving towards your face should give some bonus.<br /> <br /> Same goes for Matter, it's better to detect that the floor it's going to give *before* it does. To know that you need to judge the resistance of the floor (Matter) alongside the Forces working over it, they're interwoven that way<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see the need of correspondence, unless the mage wants to scan someplace (or someone) far away. </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure about Corr, my reasoning would be that:<br /> <br /> Corr may be necessary because all the other Spheres have a reach of &quot;clear sensory range&quot;. I think that may apply to the range you can *extend* your magical senses too (hence, a sniper would be able to shoot you w/o you noticing until the bullet get's too close to be dodged).<br /> <br /> Corr, because it isn't limited by sensory range, could be required to relegate the sensory data to a secondary plane. That is, to allow your magick to work on the invisible. \u200bIf this is the case, w/o Corr you would need to be &quot;clearly sensing&quot; how Forces move and how Matter/Life would &quot;react&quot; to that ALL the time. That's, again, asking for a penalty of sensory overload.<br /> <br /> If either of those are true, Corr would be required (or at least a very useful addition)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-11-2019, 08:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T05:33:58-08:00","id":1347662,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a>, I don't know if I got this right, what Life is doing here. There would be no sensory overload because, while there are lots of Forces in the environment all the time, they are not capable of causing harm and/or are not directed at you. Only the Forces that sre aligned with you *and* are strong enough to cause harm will tingle the sense.<br /> Also, we suffer from traffic accidents for several reasons: lack of attention, getting hit from behind/etc. That's would not happen with this power; lack of reaction, seeing/hearing but not reacting in time, in this case tjis effect should be paired with another one to increase reflexes.<br /> <br /> Also, I just thought about another scenario: thr mage is sleeping/distracted and a poisonous snake sneak to him to take a bite. In this case Forces would not help, but Life could... What you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T06:37:49-08:00","id":1347670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346889-lvl-1-spheres-effects-ideas?p=1347662#post1347662\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a>There would be no sensory overload because, while there are lots of Forces in the environment all the time, they are not capable of causing harm and/or are not directed at you. Only the Forces that sre aligned with you *and* are strong enough to cause harm will tingle the sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>How do your magick determine what it's capable of harming you w/o knowing how resistant you are? Life can connect the dots between the forces and your health, otherwise you would have to connect them by yourself somehow<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, I just thought about another scenario: thr mage is sleeping/distracted and a poisonous snake sneak to him to take a bite. In this case Forces would not help, but Life could... What you think? </div> </div> </div>Yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T08:32:36-08:00","id":1347690,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346889-lvl-1-spheres-effects-ideas?p=1347656#post1347656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not so sure about Corr, my reasoning would be that:<br /> <br /> Corr may be necessary because all the other Spheres have a reach of &quot;clear sensory range&quot;. I think that may apply to the range you can *extend* your magical senses too (hence, a sniper would be able to shoot you w/o you noticing until the bullet get's too close to be dodged).</div> </div> </div> </div>To add to this: Corr quite simply takes care of your back. While 'clear sensory range' and paradigm might actually allow you to *hear* danger behind you, not every mage takes in things that way - I wager that most Mages focus on the sensory perceptions in the most common way: eyes. Sight.<br /> <br /> So Cor 1 would make sure that that sensing at least extends to 360 degrees line of sight around you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-11T10:31:37-08:00","id":1347710,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> Oh now I see the use of Life. My initial thought was like inserting fixed parameters like &quot;any chsnge in temperature above 40\u00b0C&quot; for fireballs, or any object with a speed greater than &quot;X m/s&quot;. But your way is even better, as the parameters are continually measured and it will only &quot;tingle&quot; when something that will really hurt is coming. Very nice.<br /> <br /> Now, in the snake example, do you think it would tingle just by the presence of the snake? Or only when it tries to bite? Maybe if it is close enough to bite?<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6606_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6606\" data-vbnamecard=\"6606\">Ambrosia</a> As you said, the mage can just feel, hear, etc. the sensation. The back of the mage is still in sensory range. Just like a sonar wouldn't require Correspondence. Unless great distances are covered. But i get what you are staying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T11:03:09-08:00","id":1347961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1346889-lvl-1-spheres-effects-ideas?p=1347710#post1347710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, in the snake example, do you think it would tingle just by the presence of the snake? Or only when it tries to bite? Maybe if it is close enough to bite?</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I envisioned this, it would tingle when the snake it's about to bite.<br /> <br /> But I could see it either way, depending on how the magick it's described/worded.<br /> <br /> All have pros and cons: On one hand, reacting when a snake tries to bite may be too late for most normal people (esp. if you're not seeing the snake, but sensing a &quot;tingle&quot; or otherwise vague input). On the other hand, the more &quot;breadth&quot; you allow your senses to have, the more false positives they will catch.<br /> It does seem that having supernatural reflexes would go well with this kind of senses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}